syn_map:|DFT-100 |Info   |   10|Added DFT object.                                 |
syn_map:|DFT-185 |Info   |    1|Did not find any shift-register segment in the    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | design.                                          |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Shift registers are searched along the functional |
syn_map:|        |       |     | path. A shift register is considered a valid scan|
syn_map:|        |       |     | segment if the set, reset, and preset pins of all|
syn_map:|        |       |     | its flops are held at their inactive value and   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | the enable pin is held to its active value.      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | Ensure that test mode signals are specified for  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | the synchronous pins of the flops in the shift   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | register. Additionally, ensure that the          |
syn_map:|        |       |     | '-min_length' and '-max_length' options have     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | proper values, and that the design is not already|
syn_map:|        |       |     | scan-connected.                                  |
syn_map:|LBR-9   |Warning|   40|Library cell has no output pins defined.          |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Add the missing output pin(s)                     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | , then reload the library. Else the library cell |
syn_map:|        |       |     | will be marked as timing model i.e. unusable.    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | Timing_model means that the cell does not have   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | any defined function. If there is no output pin, |
syn_map:|        |       |     | Genus will mark library cell as unusable i.e. the|
syn_map:|        |       |     | attribute 'usable' will be marked to 'false' on  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | the libcell. Therefore, the cell is not used for |
syn_map:|        |       |     | mapping and it will not be picked up from the    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | library for synthesis. If you query the attribute|
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'unusable_reason' on the libcell; result will be:|
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'Library cell has no output pins.'Note: The      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | message LBR-9 is only for the logical pins and   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | not for the power_ground pins. Genus will depend |
syn_map:|        |       |     | upon the output function defined in the pin group|
syn_map:|        |       |     | (output pin)                                     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | of the cell, to use it for mapping. The pg_pin   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | will not have any function defined.              |
syn_map:|LBR-41  |Info   |    2|An output library pin lacks a function attribute. |
syn_map:|        |       |     |If the remainder of this library cell's semantic  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | checks are successful, it will be considered as a|
syn_map:|        |       |     | timing-model                                     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | (because one of its outputs does not have a valid|
syn_map:|        |       |     | function.                                        |
syn_map:|LBR-109 |Info   |    2|Set default library domain.                       |
syn_map:|LBR-141 |Warning|   32|Clock function definition makes cell unusable.    |
syn_map:|        |       |     |The sequential cell cannot be inferred because its|
syn_map:|        |       |     | clock function is unknown.                       |
syn_map:|LBR-155 |Info   | 4224|Mismatch in unateness between 'timing_sense'      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | attribute and the function.                      |
syn_map:|        |       |     |The 'timing_sense' attribute will be respected.   |
syn_map:|LBR-161 |Info   |    2|Setting the maximum print count of this message to|
syn_map:|        |       |     | 10 if information_level is less than 9.          |
syn_map:|LBR-162 |Info   |  248|Both 'pos_unate' and 'neg_unate' timing_sense arcs|
syn_map:|        |       |     | have been processed.                             |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Setting the 'timing_sense' to non_unate.          |
syn_map:|LBR-412 |Info   |    2|Created nominal operating condition.              |
syn_map:|        |       |     |The nominal operating condition is represented,   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | either by the nominal PVT values specified in the|
syn_map:|        |       |     | library source                                   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | (via nom_process,nom_voltage and nom_temperature |
syn_map:|        |       |     | respectively)                                    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | , or by the default PVT values (1.0,1.0,1.0).    |
syn_map:|LBR-415 |Info   |   31|Unusable library cells found at the time of       |
syn_map:|        |       |     | loading a library.                               |
syn_map:|        |       |     |For  more  information, refer to 'Cells Identified|
syn_map:|        |       |     | as Unusable' in the 'User Guide'. To know the    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | reason why a cell is considered as unusable,     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | check 'unusable_reason' libcell attribute.       |
syn_map:|LBR-518 |Info   |    2|Missing a function attribute in the output pin    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | definition.                                      |
syn_map:|PA-7    |Info   |    2|Resetting power analysis results.                 |
syn_map:|        |       |     |All computed switching activities are removed.    |
syn_map:|PHYS-129|Info   |  238|Via with no resistance will have a value of '0.0' |
syn_map:|        |       |     | assigned for resistance value.                   |
syn_map:|        |       |     |If this is the expected behavior, this message can|
syn_map:|        |       |     | be ignored.                                      |
syn_map:|PHYS-279|Warning|  192|Physical cell not defined in library.             |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Ensure that the proper library files are available|
syn_map:|        |       |     | and have been imported.                          |
syn_map:|PHYS-752|Info   |    2|Partition Based Synthesis execution skipped.      |
syn_map:|POPT-40 |Warning|    4|Setting clock-gating integrated cell on a         |
syn_map:|        |       |     | non-uniquified subdesign, which might have been  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | multiply instantiated.                           |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Use the edit_netlist dedicate_subdesign <instance>|
syn_map:|        |       |     | to uniquify the subdesign if you do not want this|
syn_map:|        |       |     | attribute to be set on all instances.            |
syn_map:|POPT-502|Warning|    6|Total power has skewed contributions from leakage |
syn_map:|        |       |     | and dynamic power.                               |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Dynamic power is typically calculated/specified   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | for some 'active period'. For combination of     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | leakage and dynamic power                        |
syn_map:|        |       |     | opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio must specify the    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | percentage of overall time for which the design  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | is not in the 'active period' but in 'idle mode',|
syn_map:|        |       |     | i.e. no dynamic power but only leakage power is  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | consumed. For a reasonable optimization across   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | dynamic and leakage power, leakage contribution  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | is expected to be above 5% and below 95%. A      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | contribution of less than 5% will result in      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | limited leakage optimization and contribution of |
syn_map:|        |       |     | more than 95% will result in limited dynamic     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | optimization. Adjust                             |
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio' so that leakage   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | contribution comes to an intermediate value if   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | you intend both optimizations to occur.          |
syn_map:|ST-136  |Warning|    2|Not obtained requested number of super thread     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | servers.                                         |
syn_map:|        |       |     |The requested number of cpus are not available on |
syn_map:|        |       |     | machine.                                         |
