prects:@flow 2: # Multi host/cpu attributes
prects:@flow 3: #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
prects:@flow 4: # The FLOWTOOL_NUM_CPUS is an environment variable which should be exported by
prects:@flow 5: # the specified dist script.  This connects the number of CPUs being reserved
prects:@flow 6: # for batch jobs with the current flow scripts.  The LSB_MAX_NUM_PROCESSORS is
prects:@flow 7: # a typical environment variable exported by distribution platforms and is
prects:@flow 8: # useful for ensuring all interactive jobs are using the reserved amount of CPUs.
prects:@flow 9: if {[info exists ::env(FLOWTOOL_NUM_CPUS)]} {
prects:@flow 10: set max_cpus $::env(FLOWTOOL_NUM_CPUS)
prects:@flow 11: }
prects:@flow 17: switch -glob {innovus} {
prects:@@flow 0: set_multi_cpu_usage -verbose -local_cpu   $max_cpus
prects:**WARN: (PRL-39):	Number of local CPUs specified (16) > Actual number of CPUs in the host (8). The lower value will be used.
